in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone
in @mirror
in @mirror/bench

# @kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone — the OPERATIONAL HALF of
# the kintsugi-on-Rust first lift. The auto-fracture that emits a
# repair morphism when dark_count regresses across kintsugi ticks.
#
# Tick 41 / first ouroboros bite (operational half). Sibling to
# @epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone (declarative half;
# landed in the same tick).
#
# === The bilateral pattern (#53; third instance) ===
#
# Per the established property+fracture bilateral pattern:
# - Declarative half: the predicate (@epistemologic/property/<name>)
# - Operational half: the fracture body via splinter(ast)
#                     (@kintsugi/fracture/<name>)
#
# The two halves compose via the kintsugi loop's active_pass: when
# the property's verdict fails on an opacity (shard at tick n+1 with
# dark_count > tick n), the fracture body emits a morphism whose
# splinter(ast) names the re-converge action the substrate-pull loop
# applies.
#
# Third instance of the pattern after:
# - First: @kintsugi/fracture/keyword (`d908798`, 2026-06-10)
# - Second: @mirror/fracture/predicate (forward-promised, #272)
# - Third: this shard
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Reads ONE opacity at a time (per the property's per-site failure
# surface). Each opacity names ONE offending tick-pair (n, n+1) where
# the substrate-pull dark_count regressed. The fracture body emits a
# morphism whose splinter(ast) names:
#
#   - The shard being re-converged (`opacity.location.file`)
#   - The action: re-run the kintsugi loop at tick n+1 with the
#     substrate-pull gradient pointing back toward tick n's
#     dark_count (or LOWER — the substrate's proof requires
#     non-increasing, not just equal)
#
# The morphism's content field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at @meta/ast altitude: same shard path, the substrate-pull tick
# re-run from the converged state.
#
# === Why this lift is safe ===
#
# Per Taut's analysis: today's 38-min hang did NOT regress
# dark_count — it regressed compile-time. So this fracture body's
# emit-on-regress path won't fire on today's substrate state. The
# bilateral pair lands clean; primes the next lift
# (cold_compile_within_tolerance) which WOULD have caught today.
#
# === Composes with @mirror/bench ===
#
# This fracture body's emitted morphism feeds @mirror/bench's
# regress_check action via composition. When the kintsugi loop
# applies the morphism, bench records the runtime of the re-converge
# as a new crystal in the predecessor-chain. The chain walks back
# through the regression to the last known-good state.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Hoare-logic loop invariants  the classical discipline of
#                                proving termination via a ranking
#                                function. dark_count IS the ranking
#                                function; this fracture body IS the
#                                substrate-pull repair action.
#   shrinking counterexamples    QuickCheck's discipline of reducing
#                                a failing case to the smallest
#                                counterexample. The fracture body
#                                emits a shrunk repair morphism.
#   ranking-function repair      structural-recursion termination
#                                proofs in Coq/Agda; this body lifts
#                                that discipline to substrate-decl
#                                altitude.
#
# Spec context: shards/epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#               (the DECLARATIVE HALF this fracture body composes);
#               shards/mirror/bench.mirror (the bench substrate-decl
#               this fracture body's morphism feeds via compose).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]] (#87;
#                       this fracture body is the operational half of
#                       the first ouroboros bite),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53 pattern; this is the operational half of
#                       the third instance),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                       (the substrate's parametric AST-fragment
#                       construction; this body discharges via
#                       splinter(ast) declaratively, no Rust),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity, morphism,
#                       splinter(ast) are typed carriers).
# Related shards: epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#                  (the property this fracture body operationalizes),
#                 mirror/bench.mirror (the bench substrate-decl whose
#                  regress_check feeds back to the chain walk),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi loop
#                  driver; active_pass reads this fracture body when
#                  composing the per-pulse candidate morphism_set),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                  `location`, `transparency`, `verdict`,
#                  `splinter(ast)`),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the morphism carrier this
#                  body emits; `query_phi` is the gate the emitted
#                  morphism flows through),
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the `morphism_context`
#                  carrier; the per-candidate slice the loop pairs
#                  this fracture's morphism with its pre-anchor),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (FIRST INSTANCE
#                  of the bilateral pattern; this shard is the THIRD).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/floyd-hoare-1969
source @arxiv/programming/claessen-hughes-2000

glass @kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone {
  focus dark_count_monotone
  project dark_count_monotone
  split dark_count_monotone
  shift dark_count_monotone
  settle dark_count_monotone
}

# === resolve_dark_count_regression action (fracture body) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone
# altitude. Reads an opacity (one element of
# `dark_count_monotone(shard, n, np1).failure(opacity_map)`'s
# opacity_map); emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop
# proposes through `query_phi`.
#
# The morphism's content field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at @meta/ast altitude: same shard path, re-converge action. The
# substrate's compiler verifies the construction is deterministic
# and well-typed.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE per substrate-pull-correct via
# splinter(ast) (declared at shards/glass.mirror's tick-2 carrier).
# Per [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]: splinter(ast) IS
# the substrate's quote primitive; the re-converge action rides the
# same carrier as every other AST rewrite. No Rust AST manipulation;
# no obligation block at this altitude (the splinter(ast) body itself
# is the discharge).
#
# Per `splinter(ast)`'s parametric specialisation: the record IS its
# content-addressed handle. The morphism's content ref collapses to
# the substrate-pull-correct re-converge action.
resolve_dark_count_regression(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/dark_count_monotone
out resolve_dark_count_regression
